     ddeevvmmaattcchh — print information about unattached devices

SSYYNNOOPPSSIISS
     ddeevvmmaattcchh [--aa | ----aallll] [--dd | ----dduummpp] [[--hh | ----hhiinnttss] _f_i_l_e]
              [[--pp | ----nnoommaattcchh] _e_v_e_n_t] [--qq | ----qquuiieett] [--uu | ----uunnbboouunndd]
              [--vv | ----vveerrbboossee]

DDEESSCCRRIIPPTTIIOONN
     The ddeevvmmaattcchh utility, without any arguments, prints all the kernel mod‐
     ules it has found for all the unattached, enabled devices in the system.

     --aa ----aallll              Include all devices, not just the ones that are un‐
                           attached.

     --dd ----dduummpp             Produce a human readable dump of the _l_i_n_k_e_r_._h_i_n_t_s
                           file.

     --hh ----hhiinnttss _f_i_l_e       Use the named _f_i_l_e instead of _l_i_n_k_e_r_._h_i_n_t_s guessed
                           from the current module load path.

     --pp ----nnoommaattcchh _e_v_e_n_t    Parse and use a standard NOMATCH event from devd(8)
                           for matching instead of searching the device tree.

     --qq ----qquuiieett            Suppress some error messages and simply return a
                           non-zero exit code.  This is helpful to avoid an
                           endless list of warnings during bootup if no hints
                           are available.

     --uu ----uunnbboouunndd          Attempt to produce a list of those drivers with PNP
                           info whose driver tables with that PNP info cannot
                           be found.

     --vv ----vveerrbboossee          Produce more verbose output.

