BBUUGGSS
     The kernel has hints in it, but we exclude it from the list of modules to
     suggest for unmatched devices.  We exclude it when suggesting drivers,
     but include it when looking for unbound devices or producing a full dump
     of _l_i_n_k_e_r_._h_i_n_t_s.  This can be confusing.

     Some modules are hard links in _/_b_o_o_t_/_k_e_r_n_e_l and will be reported twice.

     The PNP string's attributes are evaluated once per PNP entry on that bus
     rather than once.

     The term PNP is overloaded in FreeBSD.  It means, generically, the iden‐
     tifying data the bus provides about a device.  While this include old ISA
     PNP identifiers, it also includes the logical equivalent in USB, PCI, and
     others.

     Many drivers currently lack proper PNP table decorations and need to be
     updated.

